1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,820
In 1920, a Boston clerk found a loophole in the mail.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,710
Buy this postal coupon in Italy for pennies.

3
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:10,320
Trade it in America for stamps worth more.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,920
Charles Ponzi promised investors 50% in 45 days.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,680
By summer, a quarter million dollars poured in every day.

6
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,510
But he barely bought any coupons.

7
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:23,920
New money paid old investors.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,710
His promises needed 160 million coupons.

9
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:30,320
About 27,000 existed.

10
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,210
By August, it collapsed.

11
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:34,460
The scheme still bears his name.
